Id: inet006w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_inetd
Fix: Remove the telnet, rsh or TFTP server package; SSH does the same job encrypted.
References: in.telnetd(8); rshd(8); in.tftpd(8); CIS Distribution Independent Linux Benchmark 2.2 (Special Purpose Services)
Controls: CIS 2.3, 4.8; NIST CM-7; ISO 8.19, 8.21; CE Secure configuration

A telnet, rsh/rlogin/rexec or TFTP server program is installed (under
/usr/sbin or its neighbours) though nothing enables it today: no
systemd unit, no xinetd or inetd entry while that super-server is
enabled, no running process. It is one 'systemctl enable' from use,
and an intruder with root finds a cleartext login server ready for his
return. The detail names the program, and any dormant xinetd.d or
inetd.conf entry that would serve it if the super-server were turned
on.

Installed is judged by the program being there, not by the package
database: the configuration a removed package leaves behind is not a
server, and a binary copied in is. The clients (telnet, rsh, tftp) are
not judged: Debian installs a telnet client on every standard system,
and a client gives an attacker nothing nc or python does not. Remove
the server package.
